description:
About the job

In this role, the primary responsibility is to contribute to sales growth within the assigned territory by supporting and executing multiple stages of the sales process (both direct and indirect) as our new Inside Sales Specialist!

Key Responsibilities


Support the Peel 3D sales team in preparing quotes, proposals, and required sales documentation; 
For direct sales: manage and follow up on sales opportunities, and organize web-based product demonstrations when needed;
For indirect sales: follow up with distributors to support and advance sales activities; 
Coordinate closely with production, logistics, and finance to ensure smooth order processing through to delivery; 
Prepare and maintain accurate sales documentation throughout the sales cycle; 
Build and sustain strong, professional relationships with customers and partners; 
Maintain and update price lists to ensure accuracy and consistency; 
Ensure proper use of Salesforce CRM, adhering to established processes, data quality standards, and best practices; 
Facilitate internal communication within the sales team and contribute to continuous improvement of sales processes, tools, and strategies. 


What Will Help You Succeed At FARO CREAFORM


Have a degree in business, administration, engineering or relevant field; 
3-5 years of experience in sales in a manufacturing/technological environment; 
Have a strong interest for high technology and towards learning about technological products. 
Have minimum experience in a technical field, sales and/or customer support;
Demonstrated ability and willingness to use AI tools to improve productivity, decision-making, work quality, and to reduce costs. 
The successful candidate must be able to identify appropriate AI use cases and critically evaluate AI-generated outputs.
Be results-oriented; 
Being bilingual (English-Spanish) is essential for internal and external communication; 


Here’s What We Offer You


Growth opportunities within a global organization
Continuous training and coaching to support your development
A supportive and collaborative team environment
Flexible work schedules
A human, innovative, and forward-thinking company culture


Compensation

Currency: MXN

Salary Minimum: Market

Salary Maximum: Market

Incentive: Yes

Disclaimer: Where a specific pay range is noted, it is a good faith estimate at the time of this posting. The actual salary offered will be based on experience, skills, qualifications, market / business considerations, and geographic location.

AMETEK, Inc. is a leading global provider of industrial technology solutions serving a diverse set of attractive niche markets with annual sales over $7.5 billion.

AMETEK is committed to making a safer, sustainable, and more productive world a reality. We use differentiated technology solutions to solve our customers’ most complex challenges. We employ 22,000 colleagues, in 35 countries, that are grounded by our core values: Ethics and Integrity, Respect for the Individual, Inclusion, Teamwork, and Social Responsibility. AMETEK is a component of the S&P 500. Visit https://www.ametek.com/careers for more information.
